  {
    "id": "gate-algorithms-test-1-q002",
    "exam": {
      "name": "GATE",
      "fullName": "Graduate Aptitude Test in Engineering",
      "year": null,
      "session": "Algorithms"
    },
    "question": {
      "pdfName": "Algorithms_4.pdf",
      "direction": "Directions for questions 1 to 25: Select the correct alternative from the given choices.",
      "text": "Let M be an integer greater than 1. Which of the following represents the order of growth of the expression \\(\\sum_{i=1}^{n} M^i\\) as a function of ‘n’?",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "\\(\\Theta(n^M)\\)"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "\\(\\Theta(M^{2n+1})\\)"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "\\(\\Theta(M^n \\log n)\\)"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "\\(\\Theta(M^n)\\)"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "D",
      "correctText": "\\(\\Theta(M^n)\\)",
      "explanation": "Let M value be ‘3’\n\n\\(\\sum_{i=1}^{n} 3^i = 3^1 + 3^2 + 3^3 + ... + 3^n\\)\n\nThe sequence is in Geometric Progression.\nFirst term = 3 = a\n\\(r = \\frac{3^2}{3} = 3\\)\n\nAs r > 1 ⇒ sum = \\(a\\frac{r^n-1}{r-1}\\)\n\n\\(3\\frac{(3^n-1)}{3-1} = \\frac{3(3^n-1)}{2}\\)\n\\(= \\frac{3\\cdot3^n-3\\cdot1}{2} = \\frac{3^{n+1}-3^1}{2}\\)\n\n\\(=3^{n+1} \\Rightarrow 3^n\\) (Ignore constants in Asymptotic Notations)\n\n∴ \\(\\Theta(M^n)\\) is the order of growth of given expression.\nChoice (D)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
    "classification": {
      "subject": "Algorithms",
      "topic": "Asymptotic Analysis",
      "subtopic": null,
      "tags": []
    },
    "source": {
      "type": "practice_test",
      "organization": null,
      "documentTitle": "Algorithms_4.pdf",
      "url": null,
      "page": 1
    },
