  {
    "id": "gate-algorithms-test-1-q003",
    "exam": {
      "name": "GATE",
      "fullName": "Graduate Aptitude Test in Engineering",
      "year": null,
      "session": "Algorithms"
    },
    "question": {
      "pdfName": "Algorithms_4.pdf",
      "direction": "Directions for questions 1 to 25: Select the correct alternative from the given choices.\n\nCommon Data For Questions 3 and 4:\nTo compute the Matrix product M1 M2, where M1 has ‘p’ rows and ‘q’ columns and M2 has ‘q’ rows and ‘r’ columns, takes time proportional to ‘pqr’, and result is a matrix of ‘p’ rows and ‘r’ columns. Consider the given 5 matrices, A1, A2, A3, A4, and A5 and their dimensions are P0 × P1, P1 × P2, P2 × P3, P3 × P4, P4 × P5, respectively. The values are P0 = 10, P1 = 5, P2 = 15, P3 = 20, P4 = 40, P5 = 25.",
      "text": "MATRIX-CHAIN-ORDER computes the rows from bottom to top and from left to right, The value of X (where X = M[1, 2]) is ________",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "600"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "750"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "800"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "900"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null,
      "image": "images/Algorithms_4/algorithms_4-q003-question.png"
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "B",
      "correctText": "750",
      "explanation": "Computing the matrix product A_i...k A_k+1...j takes P_i−1 P_k P_j scalar multiplications.\nM[i, j] = { 0 if i = j; min_{i ≤ k < j} {M[i, k] + M[k + 1, j] + P_{i−1} P_k P_j}, if i < j }\n\nX = M[1, 2]\ni = 1, j = 2\nk = 1 (∵ i ≤ k < j)\nP0 = 10, P1 = 5, P2 = 15, P3 = 20, P4 = 40, P5 = 25\nM[1, 1] = 0\nM[2, 2] = 0\nM[3, 3] = 0\nM[4, 4] = 0\nM[5, 5] = 0\nM[1, 2] = min_{i ≤ k < j} [M[i, k] + M[k + 1, j] + P_{i−1} P_k P_j]\n\nK = 1 ⇒ M[1, 2] = M[1, 1] + M[2, 2] + P0 P1 P2\n0 + 0 + 10 × 5 × 15\n= 750\nChoice (B)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
    "classification": {
      "subject": "Algorithms",
      "topic": "Dynamic Programming",
      "subtopic": null,
      "tags": []
    },
    "source": {
      "type": "practice_test",
