  {
    "id": "gate-algorithms-test-1-q004",
    "exam": {
      "name": "GATE",
      "fullName": "Graduate Aptitude Test in Engineering",
      "year": null,
      "session": "Algorithms"
    },
    "question": {
      "pdfName": "Algorithms_4.pdf",
      "direction": "Directions for questions 1 to 25: Select the correct alternative from the given choices.\n\nCommon Data For Questions 3 and 4:\nTo compute the Matrix product M1 M2, where M1 has ‘p’ rows and ‘q’ columns and M2 has ‘q’ rows and ‘r’ columns, takes time proportional to ‘pqr’, and result is a matrix of ‘p’ rows and ‘r’ columns. Consider the given 5 matrices, A1, A2, A3, A4, and A5 and their dimensions are P0 × P1, P1 × P2, P2 × P3, P3 × P4, P4 × P5, respectively. The values are P0 = 10, P1 = 5, P2 = 15, P3 = 20, P4 = 40, P5 = 25.",
      "text": "The value of Y (where Y = M[2, 4]) is ________.",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "1500"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "5500"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "15000"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "None of the above"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null,
      "image": "images/Algorithms_4/algorithms_4-q004-question.png"
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "B",
      "correctText": "5500",
      "explanation": "M[2, 4] → The possible values for ‘K’ are 2, 3.\n(1) M[2, 4] = M[2, 2] + M[3, 4] + P1 P2 P4, k = 2\n(2) M[2, 4] = M[2, 3] + M[4, 4] + P1 P3 P4, k = 3\n\nWe need to get the values of M[3, 4] and M[2, 3]\nM[3, 4] = M[3, 3] + M[4, 4] + P2 P3 P4, k = 3\n0 + 0 + 15 × 20 × 40 = 12000\nM[2, 3] = M[2, 2] + M[3, 3] + P1 P2 P3, k = 2\n= 0 + 0 + 5 × 15 × 20\n= 1500\n\nChoose min of (1) and (2)\nM[2, 4] = M[2, 2] + M[3, 4] + P1 P2 P4, k = 2\n0 + 12000 + 5 × 15 × 40\n= 12000 + 3000 = 15000\nM[2, 4] = M[2, 3] + M[4, 4] + P1 P3 P4, k = 3\n= 1500 + 0 + 5 × 20 × 40\n= 1500 + 4000 = 5500\n∴ M[2, 4] = min{15000, 5500} = 5500\nChoice (B)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
