    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "D",
      "correctText": "I–False, II–False",
      "explanation": "I. f(n) = O(g(n)) and g(n) = O(h(n)) then f(n) = Ω(h(n))\nLets assume\nf(n) = n\ng(n) = n²\nh(n) = n³\nf(n) ≤ g(n)\n⇒ n ≤ n²\ng(n) ≤ h(n) ⇒ n² ≤ n³\nThen f(n) ≥ h(n)\n⇒ n ≥ n³ (false)\n\nII. T(n) = T(n − 2) + 1\nGives O(n) time complexity (False)\nChoice (D)",
      "status": "confirmed"
